  "scope": "The full existential counterexample of Federer 3.2.24, p. 260: actual Borel W,Z in R4 have zero naturally normalized H2 mass and finite (H^2,2) rectifiability, but their Cartesian product has infinite naturally normalized H4 mass. Both product conclusions of 3.2.23 are explicitly disproved; the reference product is zero on every test subset, and the first factor is not genuinely 2-rectifiable.",
  "proof_route": "Specialize the actual interleaved Cantor sets of 2.10.29 to scalar exponent 1/4 and fourth powers. Finite natural H1 factor masses imply zero H2 masses by 2.10.2. The mixed product has infinite H4 mass because 4<4(1+1/4)=5, through the existing orthogonal coordinate identification. A proved natural-exponent adapter identifies the real power gauge with actual unit-ball coefficient and existing Hausdorff measure via opaque cost laws and uniqueness; no Gamma identity or fractional dimension-drop hypothesis. Finite coordinate powers preserve Borelness. Null factors are finite measure rectifiable via the empty rectifiable cover. Infinite product mass disproves finite product rectifiability and any proposed full-measure identity.",
